{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00279",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 3.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Okay, good morning. Come in, have a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.64,
      "end_seconds": 6.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Evening, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 7.21,
      "end_seconds": 10.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.68,
      "end_seconds": 13.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "In your own words, what's happened?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.01,
      "end_seconds": 20.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "I wanted to get severe pain in my right side that comes in waves looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.79,
      "end_seconds": 23.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.15,
      "end_seconds": 30.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "For one week, I'd say. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.18,
      "end_seconds": 33.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.34,
      "end_seconds": 37.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Okay, so it sort of comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.31,
      "end_seconds": 44.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.81,
      "end_seconds": 48.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.42,
      "end_seconds": 57.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, and nausea. That's been about the same, one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.47,
      "end_seconds": 60.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Any blood in the urine as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.92,
      "end_seconds": 66.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Yeah. About two weeks, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.67,
      "end_seconds": 68.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "What about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.81,
      "end_seconds": 71.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "No. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 72.62,
      "end_seconds": 76.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.27,
      "end_seconds": 83.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.43,
      "end_seconds": 91.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. And difficulty passing urine, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.68,
      "end_seconds": 93.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "No, no difficulty passing urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.39,
      "end_seconds": 98.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Any burning when passing urine, previous kidney stones or testicular pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.76,
      "end_seconds": 110.75,
      "duration_seconds": 11.99,
      "text": "No, no burning when passing urine, no previous kidney stones, no testicular pain. I did have pain moving down to the groin at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.09,
      "end_seconds": 114.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.75,
      "end_seconds": 117.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.23,
      "end_seconds": 121.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.02,
      "end_seconds": 124.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 125.77,
      "end_seconds": 133.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature 36.7, pulse 112, oxygen saturation is 96 percent. Blood pressure 116 over 83."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.54,
      "end_seconds": 139.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Alright, good, thank you. Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.56,
      "end_seconds": 140.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.96,
      "end_seconds": 145.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.75,
      "end_seconds": 151.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Yes, codeine, it gives me feeling very drowsy. I'm allergic to aspirin, I get wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.74,
      "end_seconds": 156.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.3,
      "end_seconds": 175.61,
      "duration_seconds": 17.31,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for five years. Gout, for about ten years. I've had diabetes, yes. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.17,
      "end_seconds": 178.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.74,
      "end_seconds": 182.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "I, I have an enlarged prostate, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.55,
      "end_seconds": 190.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.43,
      "end_seconds": 194.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "It's amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 195.11,
      "end_seconds": 199.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 2.5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.41,
      "end_seconds": 204.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.07,
      "end_seconds": 208.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.22,
      "end_seconds": 215.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.03,
      "end_seconds": 219.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.37,
      "end_seconds": 236.53,
      "duration_seconds": 16.16,
      "text": "For the gout, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Uh, you know, I'm on glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. I'm on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.94,
      "end_seconds": 240.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.54,
      "end_seconds": 247.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "No, it's at home. I was on Glycomet before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.54,
      "end_seconds": 249.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.16,
      "end_seconds": 254.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Well, my sister has thyroid problems. My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.91,
      "end_seconds": 255.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.61,
      "end_seconds": 258.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.12,
      "end_seconds": 260.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.29,
      "end_seconds": 262.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.82,
      "end_seconds": 266.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.41,
      "end_seconds": 268.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.33,
      "end_seconds": 271.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.78,
      "end_seconds": 287.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the right loin when I tap, and your tummy is soft."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.88,
      "end_seconds": 313.18,
      "duration_seconds": 20.3,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like a kidney stone. I can't rule out a muscular back pain yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.18,
      "end_seconds": 316.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.46,
      "end_seconds": 340.02,
      "duration_seconds": 18.56,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a kidney stone, and we'll know more once the an ultrasound of the kidneys is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had severe pain in your right side that comes in waves for one week, and no burning when passing urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.86,
      "end_seconds": 342.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.31,
      "end_seconds": 362.8,
      "duration_seconds": 19.49,
      "text": "Let's get an ultrasound of the kidneys, for flank pain. We should do a CT scan of the kidneys and bladder for suspected renal colic. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm going to order kidney function tests, for renal colic. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.31,
      "end_seconds": 390.22,
      "duration_seconds": 25.91,
      "text": "I'll start you on paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. It's for pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Drink three litres of water a day and try to strain your urine so we can catch the stone if it passes. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.05,
      "end_seconds": 401.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. I'll also refer you to the urology team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.73,
      "end_seconds": 403.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.72,
      "end_seconds": 411.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.62,
      "end_seconds": 413.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.47,
      "end_seconds": 424.26,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you get a fever or can't pass urine at all, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.72,
      "end_seconds": 428.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Okay, so got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.75,
      "end_seconds": 434.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.07,
      "end_seconds": 440.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "So, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.18,
      "end_seconds": 445.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.03,
      "end_seconds": 448.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.56,
      "end_seconds": 450.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}